skill: linkedin-post-writer
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for linkedin-post-writer. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-linkedin-post, "Write a LinkedIn post about how deleting a feature taught us to watch behavior, not requests.", "reads brand-profile and voice first|opens with a first line that wins the '…see more' tap within the cutoff|formats the body for dwell (whitespace, short paragraphs, scannable)|delivers a real lesson on-voice at a LinkedIn register|closes with a genuine discussion question and at most one soft CTA|routes any link to the first comment, not the body"
  - see-more-hook, Give me a strong opening line for a LinkedIn post about our pricing change., the first line creates curiosity/stakes within ~140 characters|does NOT open with 'I'm excited/thrilled to announce' or a greeting|earns the '…see more' expand on its own
  - avoid-cringe-pushback, Write me a broetry-style post with 'Comment YES if you agree' at the end to farm engagement., "declines the engagement-bait/broetry approach|explains briefly why it underperforms and risks credibility (LinkedIn down-ranks bait)|delivers a genuinely strong post that earns engagement honestly instead|ends on a real question, not 'Comment YES'"
  - link-in-comments, Write a LinkedIn post driving people to our new blog post (here's the link)., does NOT put the external link in the post body|routes the link to the first comment and says 'link in comments'|keeps the post native and makes the click worth it
  - personal-vs-company, Should this go on our company page or my personal profile?, recommends the personal/founder profile for thought leadership (better reach + trust)|notes when the company page is appropriate (announcements/brand)|may suggest a personal post alongside a company announcement for reach
  - reads-voice-no-fanfare, Write a LinkedIn post announcing our new feature., "uses no exclamation marks and does not say 'thrilled to announce'|leads with the benefit or a hook, not fanfare|stays on-voice at a LinkedIn register"
  - dwell-formatting, Here's a dense paragraph — make it a LinkedIn post., "breaks it into short, scannable paragraphs with whitespace for dwell|does NOT use broetry (one dramatic fragment per line for effect)|keeps a clear build from hook to payoff to question"
  - no-fabricated-story, Make up an emotional story about a customer to get reach., refuses to fabricate a fake parable or emotional story|offers to tell a real story or use a format that fits what's actually true|does not invent unverifiable claims or results
